        <head>Church Notices.</head>
        <p>Church Notices.</p>
        <p>WYCLIFFE CONGREGATIONAL CHURCH, BEWSEY-ST., WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEBRUARY 6th. 10.30 a.m.: Rev. C. P. PITT, B.A. 6.30 p.m.: Rev. JOHN YONGE. ' 7.45 p.m.: COMMUNION SERVICE. 3.0 p.m.: P.S.A. FOR MEN.</p>
        <p>BOLD-STREET WESLEYAN CHURCH. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). FEB. 6th. 10.30 a.m.: Rev. W. T. DERRY, M.A. 6.30 p.m.: Rev. P. INESON. Subject: Missing the Target." Anthem: " Come unto Him" (Gounod). BEWSEY-ROAD WESLEYAN CiltißCH. GUILD FESTIVAL. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEB. 6th. Preacher: Bet'. E. B. KEELING. - 10.30 a.m.: "The Challenge of the Future." 6.30 Dan. "Credulity changed to Faith." AFTERNOON, 2.45. MUSICAL SERVICE. Soloists: Madam LILY FAIRHURST, M. J. SEPHTON, and Mr. W. H. RIGBY. Anthems by the Choir. • Chairman: HIS WORSHIP THE MAYOR, Alderman.P. Peacock, J.P. Speaker: Alderman A. BENNETT. J.P. MONDAY EVENING, FEBRUARY 7th, E. B. KEELING will Lecture on ‘"V PRUSSIA WAS MANUFACTURED." Chairman: C. E. PARKER, Esq., J.P. BAPTIST CHURCH, LATCHFORD. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEB. 6th. Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6: Memorial Service. Mr. R. H. JACKSON, Manchester Baptist College. CIAIRO-STREET CHAPEL, WARRINGTON. ‘...) TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEB. 6th. Preacher: Rev. IRVINE LISTER. , 10.30 a.m.: Architects of Fate." 6.30 p.m.: "The Greatest Thing in the World." A Hearty Invitation Given to All. CHRISTADELPHIAN MEETING ROOM, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON.—Free Bible Address SUNDAY NEXT, at 6.30 p.m. Subject: "The Great War and its Relation to the Gospel Jesus Preached." Mr. J. E. BAMFORD, of Oldham.</p>
        <p>Cl OLBORNE-STREET BAPTIST CHURCH. N..X TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEB. 6th. Preacher: Rev. H. OGDEN. Morning, 10.45: " The Church One 'Family." Evening, 6.30: "The Inexplicable in Daily Life." Soloist: Miss ELSIE HEWITT. PRIMITIVE METHODIST CHURCH, LEGH-STREET, WARRINGTON. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY). FEBRUARY 6th. -Morning, 10.30. Evening, 6.30. Rev. A. J. CHESSUbi. - Evening subject: "Devotion from an unexpected Source." Evening Soloist: Miss MAY ISHERWOOD. Anthem:"The Radiant Morn" (Woodward). Organ Recital, 6 to 6.30 by Mr. F. H. BANNEX. ST. JOHN'S PRESBYTERIAN CHURCH, WILDERSPOOL CAUSEWAY. TO-MORROW (SUNDAY), FEBRUARY 6th. Morning, 10.46. Evening, 6.30. Preacher: Rev. W. REID.</p>
