        <p>gave a recitation entitled "The Soldier's Par- don." Two duets by the Misses Ardern and Lewis and Messrs. Walker and Lewis respect- ively, earned encores. Short speech2s were de- livered by the Pastor and Messrs. Holt, Willan, Bladen, Barrett, Smith and Hewitt, all of whom paid tribute to the work of the choir and the friends who had made the affair a success. During the evening a presentation of a beauti- ful silver cruet was made to Mrs. Turner, who, until her recent marriage, had been a member of the church choir.</p>
