        <p>KILLS PAIN</p>
        <p>Sold by all Chemists, 111 i and 213.</p>
        <p>GRAPPENHALL.</p>
        <p>Independent Methodist Church.—A well-at- tended social was held at the above place of worship on Thursday in aid of the Building Funds. The opening concert, which was miich enjoyed, was given by local talent, Mr. Mason officiating as •chairman. The artistes were Miss Gough, Mr. Plant, Miss Baker, Mr. Gifford, Mr. Leah, Miss Mason, Miss Lewis, Mr. Wood and Mrs. Plant. At 9 p.m. refreshments were provided, after which the evening Was spent in games. 'Mr: Albinson was in charge of them. A substantial sum was raised for the funds.</p>
        <p>Mr. H. E. Girvan, 32, Adelaide Road, Kensington, Liver pool, writes: " Dr. Sloan's Liniment is the very best thing I have tried for Sciatica. I was suffering, from awful pains in the back, and the third application drove all the pains out of my body. It is indeed a wonderful remedy.'</p>
        <p>Sloan's Liniment is invaluable for stoppin muscular or nerve pain of any kind. Try it at onc if you suffer with Rheumatism, Lumbago, Sore Throat, Pain in the Chest, Sprains, Bruises, etc It is also excellent for Neuralgia and Headache</p>
