        <p>- . W#RRINGTON, Numbered 14, Boit-street, and 2, Museum-street, now in the occiwation of Dr. Reginald Starkey Smith. • MR. ROBERT LOWE will offer this property for SALE on the premises, subject to con- ditions which will be then read. , The House was built for, is specially fitted, and has always been used as a doctor's resi- dence. The premises contain: Hall with tiled floor, 21ft. x 6ft.: Dining-room, 18ft. x 16ft.; Drawing-room, 21ft. x. 16ft., with china closet; Consulting-room. 16ft. x 15ft.; 'Waiting Hall, 16ft. x 9ft.; Surgery, 12ft. x 10ft., fitted with sink, &amp;c.; Butler's Pantry, with sink, hot and cold water service; Billiard-room, 26ft. x 18ft., with store cupboard; Small Storeroom; Kitchen, 21ft. x 13ft.' with 2 Store and China Cupboards and large Cooking Range; Back Kitchen, 14ft. x Bft., with closed Cooking Stove; Washhouse, Larder, Cellars with concrete floors, Wine Store with stone bins, &amp;c. First Floor.—Study, Linen Store, Nursery, 4 large Bedrooms, Bathroom, with lavatory, hot and cold water supply, and separate W.c. Upper Floor.-3 Bedrooms, Tank-room and large Attics. Outside.—W.c. Boothouse. Coalhouse, Pigeon Loft, Firewood Store, 2-stall Stable, loose Box, Harness-room, Coachhouse or Garage, all con- crete floors and Hayloft over all; large paved Yard, large Garden. The House and Outbuildings are fitted with gas and electric service. The tenure is leasehold for 999 years. from 25th March, 1872; ground rent, .08 9s. 10d. Vacant possession will be given. For further particulars apply to the Auctioneer, 5. Buttermarket-street, Warrington (Telephone No. 55); Messrs. Macdonald and Stacey, Solicitors. 2 and 3, Norfolk-street, Strand, Lcindon, W.C.i or ROBERT DAVIES &amp; CO., Solicitors, Market Place, Warrington.</p>
