        <p>SOLDIERS. ON FARMS. War Office Notice To Farmers. The Board of Agriculture and Fisheries have issued a notice to farniers announcing that in view of the sbortage of agricultural labour ar- rangements have been made with the Army Council for a limited number of soldiers serving at honk and accustomed to work on farms to be given furlough for farm work. " The farmer must pay each soldier 4s. a day or 2s. 6d. a day if board and lodging is pro- vided. Application for soldier labour must be. made t a labour exchange. Convalseeent sol- dierS may also be engaged at rates 'of 3s. 64. daily or 2s. with -board and lodging provided.</p>
